8864:# (wave 29b, E7) A group that holds members of a `plan` is limited by the plan too: the plan's own
8865:# "parallel" value (default 1) caps it, and a label without a "parallel" value of its own takes its
8866:# plan's - so {"parallel": {"zai": 2}} lets a codex ZAI member and a claude ZAI-claude member run
8867:# at once, and without it they run one after another.
8868:# { Groups (object[] of { Labels (string[]); Limit; Positions (int[] roster positions) });
8869:#   GroupOf (hashtable roster position -> group index); Cap; Effective (the most members
8870:#   that can run at once); Text ('at once' | 'one after another' | 'at most <k> at a time');
